00:26:47.319 --> 00:26:50.179
The application layering, it's a very simple architecture.

00:26:50.179 --> 00:26:51.639
It's a layered architecture.

00:26:51.640 --> 00:26:56.540
So it basically creates a bunch of components that are organized in a layered fashion.

00:26:57.080 --> 00:27:00.420
The layer on the top is the layer that the user interacts with.

00:27:00.860 --> 00:27:06.200
And then the layer on the top usually relies on a layer below to provide different kinds of services.

00:27:06.580 --> 00:27:12.320
And the layer below relies on another layer that sits another level below the current layer.

00:27:12.840 --> 00:27:13.040
Okay.

00:27:13.840 --> 00:27:20.600
So in the case of the application layering architecture, there exists three layers.

00:27:20.599 --> 00:27:22.839
and each layer has a specific responsibility.

00:27:23.679 --> 00:27:28.839
And most computer science applications can be organized in these three layers.

00:27:29.199 --> 00:27:29.299
Okay?

00:27:30.219 --> 00:27:33.719
So let's start with the first layer on the top.

00:27:33.799 --> 00:27:35.959
This is the layer that the user will interact with.

00:27:36.059 --> 00:27:38.839
This is typically called the application interface layer.

00:27:39.259 --> 00:27:45.439
So your program needs to have a layer that encodes the logic of implementing the application interface.

00:27:45.980 --> 00:27:49.339
Now, the application interface can be implemented in various ways.

00:27:49.339 --> 00:27:51.259
You can have a graphical user interface.

00:27:51.480 --> 00:27:53.319
